                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "One of the most boring HOPA games I’ve played. I don’t have very high expectations for this genre, I need it to be pretty, entertaining and pleasant. Unfortunately, The Lost Hope is none of the above. The story is not logical nor interesting, feels like written as a joke during the lunch break. Plot is full of holes and inconsequent, and when you add a poorly made voice over with ridiculously childish dialogues you get an annoying story that you can’t get into, even if you try.\nGraphics is ok, music is fine, navigation is intuitive, there is an interactive map and all the things players expect from never HOPA games. There is a bonus chapter, collectibles and the whole gameplay is around 3-3.5 hours. It is sad that the story ruins it all.\n\nI have finished the whole game with the bonus chapter only to write a review, as I don’t do that for games I haven’t finished.\n\nThe only thing I like was the zoo with cute animals, but I don’t think it’s enough to recommend the game. \n",
